# Official National Park Service web pages of Gettysburg National Military Park (www.nps.gov/gett, www.nps.gov/eise, www.nps.gov/articles): news releases of the park, the nature pages, the Little Round Top pages, student program pages and articles, fetched 2026-11-16 (page list: pages_list_2.txt; the sitemap https://www.nps.gov/sitemap.xml lists them).
# A page of an official body supports only what it literally says. A news release dates the work it announces: a fence, wall, orchard, woodlot treatment or building restoration announced there is a modern or rebuilt state (use indirect) and is never an 1863 profile; what a release says about 1863 or earlier is use direct (and, where it is a general statement that names no basis, the certainty is hedged and the tier inferred); what it says about a feature added later (a monument, tower, Camp Colt, the Cyclorama building) is use none.
# Workstream bt-web, task nps-landscape, third milestone.

